Today is Saturday.
A bright morning.
I want to see the city.
I step out of my apartment.
I see Anitha in the hallway.
"Good morning, Maya," she says.
"Good morning Anitha," I say.
"Is there a good place to walk in the city?" I ask.
"Yes, you can go to the waterfront walkway," Anitha says.
"How do I go there?" I ask.
"Walk straight out of this building," she says.
"Then turn left."
"Walk straight to the main bus stop," Anitha says.
"From there, board a bus to the city."
"In the city, ask someone the way to the waterside," she says.
I smile and thank her.
I walk straight to the gate.
And then I turn left.
I am very happy to see the city of Kochi.
